<title>MEXICO: Mexican transport minister to visit U.S.'s Slater.</title>
<headline>Mexican transport minister to visit U.S.'s Slater.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Communication and Transport Minister Carlos Ruiz Sacristan plans a working visit to the United States on Wednesday to meet his counterpart U.S. Transportation Secretary Ronald Slater, the ministry said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The two will discuss cargo and passenger transportation under the North America Free Trade Agreement (NAFTA), airport infrastructure development and telecommunications agreements between the countries, the statement said.</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
